description:
Independent pre-landing review of t3/fix-turbo-pascal-defects, head ff1e9088dc679a624bdd11a10a0c0754a446c255, baseline main 3c1ab24a. P1 seed wrong code/memory corruption. This omission is outside the diff and was reproduced using an independently rebuilt baseline seed too; no product source was edited during review.

At turbo/seed/codegen.c:2018-2024, plan_str only walks the concatenation's left operand if it is another concatenation. Its assumption that a leftmost character needs no temporary ignores embedded Length/compare/index computations. emit_concat_into:1170 evaluates that character with gen_expr, so nested string operations retain str_temp=-1 and overwrite frame locals or alias values. The new OP_LENGTH/AST_FIELD plan_val cases cannot help because this path never calls plan_val on the character.

Reproducer 1 (corpus FPC mode):

{$mode delphi}{$B+}{$H-}
program NestedLength;
var s: string;
function Check(n: integer): integer;
var u: string; sentinel: integer;
begin
 sentinel:=777;
 u:=chr(length(s+'cd'))+'ZZ';
 writeln(sentinel);
 Check:=ord(u[1])
end;
begin s:='ab'; writeln(Check(0)); writeln('done') end.

FPC 3.2.2 (-Mtp -B -O-), hosted Pascal EXE/COM and resident Pascal EXE/COM: 777 / 4 / done. Branch seed on QEMU and Bochs: 1667391748 / 4 / done. Baseline seed on QEMU: the same corruption.

Reproducer 2:

{$mode delphi}{$B+}{$H-}
program RecordCharConcat;
type Item=record c: char; end;
var r: array[0..1] of Item; s,u: string;
begin
 r[0].c:='A'; r[1].c:='B'; s:='X';
 u:=r[ord(s+'Z'='XZ')].c+'!!';
 writeln(u); writeln('done')
end.

FPC and all four Pascal paths: B!! / done; branch seed on QEMU and Bochs, and baseline seed on QEMU: A!! / done. All batches complete and CPU/reset checks are clean. This is not a deliberate char+char restriction: the right operand is a two-character string and all compilers accept both programs.

Evidence: /tmp/claude-1000/-home-tobias-Projects-InitechOS/1260bfe2-7290-4153-8f2a-6958c19d092a/scratchpad/reports/phase2/review-fix-turbo-evidence/{nested_length,record_char_concat}.pas. Full compiled/reference programs, serial captures, logs and baseline source/build are under the implementation worktree's build/turbo/review-fix/{nested,baseline-nested,baseline-tree,baseline-seed}; logs nested.log and baseline-nested.log. Review report phase2/review-fix-turbo.md.

Replay from the branch worktree (after make image and make -C turbo all): TURBO_EXEC_SOURCES='<absolute nested_length.pas> <absolute record_char_concat.pas>' TURBO_EXEC_EMULATORS='qemu bochs' TURBO_EXEC_OUT=build/turbo/review-fix/nested sh turbo/tests/execution/run.sh. Exit 1 expected: four seed comparisons fail, sixteen Pascal controls pass.

Acceptance: plan embedded scalar work in leftmost character leaves at the appropriate current temporary base, including nested concatenations and both sides of string comparisons; add these independent FPC programs to default execution coverage. Related but distinct planner entry-point omissions were initech-gnam4 and initech-hpa1h.

Reviewed 09d52a32173911debc13035096135143fefb4b2c. P1 wrong code in C seed; hosted/resident Turbo are passing controls. This is distinct from the closed record-index repeated-evaluation bug initech-uaz6c: the new index has no side effects and is evaluated once, but its string temporaries are never planned.

At turbo/seed/codegen.c:2045-2046, plan_stmt immediately returns for any whole-record assignment, without visiting either designator index. The index can contain a string comparison requiring concatenation/coercion temporaries. Those AST nodes retain str_temp=-1; cg_str_temp_offset:1070 resolves them into frame storage and aliases simultaneously live values, selecting the wrong record.
```pascal
{$mode delphi}{$B+}{$H-}
program RecordIndexString;
type Pair=record a,b: integer; end;
var r: array[0..1] of Pair; dest: Pair; s: string;
begin
 r[0].a:=10; r[0].b:=11; r[1].a:=20; r[1].b:=21; s:='X';
 dest:=r[ord(s+'Z'='XZ')];
 writeln(dest.a,' ',dest.b)
end.
```
FPC 3.2.2 (`fpc -Mtp -B -O-`, corpus Delphi/B+/H- directives): `20 21`. Seed output: `10 11`. Hosted Turbo native EXE/COM and resident Turbo native EXE/COM: `20 21`. All paths compile; QEMU and Bochs agree; both batches complete and CPU checks are green.

Reproducer: turbo/tests/review-phase2/record_index_string.pas, branch t3/review-turbo-defects. Run existing harness with TURBO_EXEC_SOURCES=turbo/tests/review-phase2/record_index_string.pas TURBO_EXEC_PATHS='seed hosted hosted-flat resident resident-flat' TURBO_EXEC_EMULATORS=bochs TURBO_EXEC_OUT=build/turbo/review-phase2/repro-record sh turbo/tests/execution/run.sh.

Also confirmed for direct field reads: plan_val's default at 1978 does not traverse AST_FIELD's array base. In record_field_string.pas, writeln(r[ord(s+'Z'='XZ')].value) prints 10 under the seed and 20 under FPC, hosted Turbo and resident Turbo on QEMU. Fixing only plan_stmt does not cover this second record-designator entry point.

Full report/evidence: /tmp/claude-1000/-home-tobias-Projects-InitechOS/1260bfe2-7290-4153-8f2a-6958c19d092a/scratchpad/reports/phase2/review-turbo.md and review-turbo-evidence/.

Reviewed 09d52a32173911debc13035096135143fefb4b2c. P1 wrong code/memory corruption in C seed only; hosted and resident Turbo are passing controls. No demonstrated impact on current K2==K3.

At turbo/seed/codegen.c:1951-1952 plan_val treats every unary operand as a scalar. OP_LENGTH actually calls gen_str_value (1427-1430); a concatenation operand requires plan_str and a reserved, numbered temporary. The missing plan leaves str_temp=-1 (ast.c:128). cg_str_temp_offset (1070-1074) then resolves it into existing frame storage. A legal Length expression silently overwrites an unrelated local:
```pascal
{$mode delphi}{$B+}{$H-}
program LengthLive;
var s: string;
function Count(n: integer): integer;
var sentinel: integer;
begin
 sentinel:=777;
 Count:=length(s+'cd');
 writeln(sentinel)
end;
begin s:='ab'; writeln(Count(0)); writeln('done') end.
```
FPC 3.2.2 (`fpc -Mtp -B -O-` with corpus Delphi/B+/H- directives): `777`, `4`, `done`. Seed compiled/run on product image: `1667391748`, `4`, `done`. Hosted Turbo native EXE/COM and resident Turbo native EXE/COM: correct output. Reproduced on QEMU and Bochs. Generated seed pf_count allocates 8 bytes, stores sentinel at [ebp-8], then uses [ebp-8] as __str_assign/__str_concat destination. The output is a real wrong-local value, not merely an emitter disagreement. A no-locals variant length_concat.pas prints correct lengths but corrupts EBP and never returns to the shell.

Reproducer: turbo/tests/review-phase2/length_live.pas, branch t3/review-turbo-defects. Run existing harness with TURBO_EXEC_SOURCES=turbo/tests/review-phase2/length_live.pas TURBO_EXEC_PATHS='seed hosted hosted-flat resident resident-flat' TURBO_EXEC_EMULATORS=bochs TURBO_EXEC_OUT=build/turbo/review-phase2/repro-length sh turbo/tests/execution/run.sh. Nonzero is expected before a fix; reference outputs come from FPC, not either product compiler.

Full report/evidence: /tmp/claude-1000/-home-tobias-Projects-InitechOS/1260bfe2-7290-4153-8f2a-6958c19d092a/scratchpad/reports/phase2/review-turbo.md and review-turbo-evidence/.

Found in the cross-provider review of cd0520da (Guard the approved Finder omissions and the frame Desktop DB seed).

flair/desktop/tests/test_frame_desktop.c:23-25:
    scene_init(&s,MOCK_DIRS,2);
    CHECK(!s.sh.windows[0].open,"loading frame preference does not open a scene");
    CHECK(finder_shell_load_views(&s.sh,bytes,(uint32_t)n)==1, ...);

The check runs on the state scene_init produced, before finder_shell_load_views reads the seed. Nothing the loader does can make it fail, so it cannot grade the claim in its message. flair/desktop/README.md also cites this test as the proof that the seed 'neither opens windows nor changes the Finder's unseeded defaults'. Verified by reading. The same file's position checks (46,115 and the 81,137 override) are sound: frame-root-position-ignored kills them semantically (reproduced, 1/1).

Fix: move the assertion after the load and check every window slot (for k < FINDER_MAX_WINDOWS: !s.sh.windows[k].open). Then show it red once with a patch that opens a window from the loader, kept as a mutant.
